A||||1||burdell1||oil leak repair
Z||000000||burdell1||08-29-99||01:02 PM||||A month or so ago I found out that my car is leaking oil from the oil pan gasket and the front cover seal. Lately it has been leaking worse so I plan on getting it fixed. However, what kind of a job is it to get at these things? Is this something I can do myself (I'm a little mechanically inclined, but not much)? Is this leak the sign that my engine is going (the mechanics said the engine had a bad knock to it)?
Z||000001||theogre||08-29-99||01:43 PM||||yes, it can be done. It's very time consuming. You likely have to remove engine mounts and support the motor from above. Dropping back of the cradle gives you a couple extra inches to access teh timing cover if you need it. You'll also need to pull out the splash skirt in the wheel well.
